{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-chi-v3-closed-form-proof-table-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:chi-v3-closed-form-proof-table-data","kind":"table","title":"Lean theorems: $\\chi_{V_3}$ closed-form identities","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-chi-v3-closed-form-proof"],"tags":["chi-V3","lean-theorems","closed-form"],"text":"chi-v3-closed-form-proof-table-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:chi-v3-closed-form-proof-table-data\"></a><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>proved statement</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_n - \\chi_p = -(q^2+1)^2 (q^2-1) / (4q)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>factored <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\leftrightarrow</code> polynomial form</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_n - \\chi_p = -(q^5 + q^3 - q - q^{-1})/4</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>split into polynomial part + geometric part</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>polynomial part vanishes at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>geometric part equals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1/4</code> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>numerical: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-75/8</code> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 2</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>vanishes at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code> (isospin invariance)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>decomposition verified at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 2</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/chi-v3-closed-form-proof-table-data.md","heading":"Table"